Revision history for Perl extension Text::JSContact

0.06  unreleased
	- writing is deterministic: the same Card gives the same bytes in
	  every process.  Text::VCardFast's hash2vcard wrote parameters in
	  Perl's hash order, so every save of an unchanged contact had a new
	  CardDAV ETag.  The module now writes content lines itself, with
	  parameters in a fixed order (PROP-ID, VALUE, TYPE, PREF, then by
	  name), folded at 75 octets without splitting a character or an
	  escape; Text::VCardFast is still the parser
	- add t/deterministic.t

0.05  2026-11-07
	- JSContact version 2.0 (RFC 9982): vcard_to_jscontact writes
	  version "2.0", and a vCard without UID gives a Card without uid
	  instead of one with a random uuid (which changed on every
	  conversion, so nothing could refer to it); jscontact_to_vcard
	  already wrote no UID for a Card without uid
	- write URI values (PHOTO, MEMBER, URL, ...) unescaped
	- read a vCard 3 inline photo once, including one whose TYPE is a list;
	  skip a Media with no uri instead of writing an empty PHOTO
	- add t/rfc9982.t

0.04  2026-10-22
	- security: strip control characters from vCard output; Text::VCardFast
	  escapes LF but writes a CR raw, so a CR in any card field could end
	  the content line early and forge extra properties.  CR and CRLF now
	  become LF (escaped as \n, or ^n in parameters) and control
	  characters other than HTAB are dropped
	- add t/injection.t

0.03  2026-10-09
	- read IMPP's RFC 9554 SERVICE-TYPE and USERNAME parameters, the ones
	  jscontact_to_vcard writes, as well as the older X-SERVICE-TYPE and
	  X-USER; an OnlineService lost its service and user on a round trip
	- an IMPP whose value is just the USERNAME (a service with no uri)
	  no longer comes back with that name as its uri
	- add t/online-services.t

0.02  2026-08-31
	- clarify licensing: same terms as Perl itself (Artistic License 1.0
	  or GPL version 1 or later)
	- include a LICENSE file in the distribution
	- add POD with NAME/AUTHOR/LICENSE (the module had none)
	- README previously claimed Artistic License 2.0, which contradicted
	  the Perl_5 metadata; the README was wrong

0.01  2026-04-05
	- Initial release
	- Bidirectional vCard <=> JSContact conversion
	- Follows RFCs 9553 (JSContact), 9554 (extensions), 9555 (vCard mapping)
	- Covers: name, emails, phones, addresses, organizations, titles,
	  anniversaries, notes, onlineServices, media, links, calendars,
	  schedulingAddresses, cryptoKeys, directories, keywords, members,
	  relatedTo, speakToAs, preferredLanguages, personalInfo
	- 192 unit tests including RFC 9555 test vectors
	- Cyrus CardDAV integration tests
